{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 7, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 american biographical drama film directed by david finch errol, written by griffin dunne, and produced by finch and daniel kagen. the film is based on the real-life story of the founding of facebook, and the subsequent lawsuits and controversies that followed.\n\nthe film stars jesse eisenberg as marc usser, the co-founder of facebook, along with andrew garfield as edward seder, and dwight honey as cambridge university's wadsworth bell. the story revolves around the founding of facebook, and the subsequent transformation of marc usser into a billionaire.\n\nthe film begins with marc usser, a college freshman, meeting edward seder, a fellow student, and the two quickly become close friends. edward is fascinated by marc's coding skills, and the two begin working together on a new website called thefacebook. as the site grows in popularity, marc and edward's friendship begins to unravel, due to differences in their personalities and expectations.\n\nthe film also explores the character of dormer, played by jason segel, who is initially part of the facebook team but eventually leaves due to disagreements with marc and edward. additionally, the film touches on the character of tyler zimmerman, played by armie hamer, who becomes increasingly bitter towards marc as facebook's popularity grows.\n\none of the standout aspects of the film is its portrayal of marc usser, who is both charismatic and infuriating. jesse eisenberg performs a remarkable portrayal of marc, capturing his intellect, arrogance, and ambition. the film's depiction of marc's rivalries and controversies is also noteworthy, as it adds depth to his character.\n\nthe film's supporting cast is equally impressive, with notable performances from andrew garfield, dwight honey, and armie hamer. the chemistry between the actors is palpable, and their portrayals of the characters add to the film's authenticity.\n\nthe direction by david finch errol is precise and measured, capturing the essence of marc usser's character and the excitement of the early days of facebook. the film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is haunting and memorable, perfectly capturing the mood and atmosphere of the film.\n\noverall, the social network is a gripping and thought-provoking film that explores the complexities of genius, ambition, and friendship. the film's portrayal of marc usser is both captivating and infuriating, and the supporting cast adds depth and nuance to the story. if you haven't seen the film before, it's definitely worth watching.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.22436656057834625}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0002536452084314078}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.03929666802287102}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0011485177092254162}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.5945353507995605}, {"token": "201", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " american", "logprob": -0.2851036787033081}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -0.011944202706217766}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": -1.847726889536716e-05}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.0005006728461012244}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -9.393251093570143e-05}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.09713417291641235}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.0010683787986636162}, {"token": " david", "logprob": -0.04422546550631523}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": -1.680836794548668e-05}, {"token": "ch", "logprob": -1.6446927785873413}, {"token": " er", "logprob": -0.39602091908454895}, {"token": "rol", "logprob": -1.278355598449707}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -1.419344425201416}, {"token": " written", "logprob": -0.4114292860031128}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -2.0146166207268834e-05}, {"token": " gr", "logprob": -1.7458332777023315}, {"token": "iffin", "logp